      "content": "Take a deep breath. It is completely normal to feel overwhelmed, but we can break this down together, one step at a time. You are capable of handling this. \n\nLet's look at line 13: 'with a wingless stone in hand'. To identify the figure of speech, let's first look at the literal meaning. Can a stone actually have wings? What is the poet suggesting by using the word 'wingless' to describe a stone?"
